VALUES
 ('GAP-310','EG','P2','OPEN','citation-verifier','energy-conservation-rest-points-seating',
  'THE DIMENSIONAL FIGURES ARE ATTRIBUTED, NOT PRIMARY-VERIFIED. Batch 3 located the primary derivation chain behind the seat and armrest dimensions REF-00953 reports, and admitted it (REF-00961..00964), but obtained ONLY Crossref bibliographic metadata - no full text was reachable for any of the four. So the corpus now knows precisely WHERE the numbers come from without having read them at source. Specifically unverified: armrest 730mm from floor at front / 250mm above seat at back / 120mm width / 120mm protrusion (attributed to Holden and Fernie, but there are TWO companion papers - Applied Ergonomics 1988 and 1989 - and the attribution is unresolved between them); seat depth 376mm (attributed to Kothiyal and Tettey, likewise split across a 2000 dataset and a 2001 design paper). These figures must not be cited as primary-sourced while they rest on REF-00953 reporting them.',
  'Falsified when the full texts are read and each figure is either confirmed at source with its clause/page, or found to differ from what REF-00953 reports - the latter being the outcome worth actively looking for, since batch 1 already found one professional-body source misreporting its own citation.',
  '2026-07-26','session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b3','2026-07-26','session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b3','ADDRESSABLE'),

 ('GAP-311','RP','P2','OPEN','multilingual-research','energy-conservation-rest-points-seating',
  'NON-ENGLISH VOCABULARY DEFERRED FOR A THIRD CONSECUTIVE BATCH. term_aliases holds no entries for this slug, so every batch has correctly declined non-EN search rather than back-translate (R11) - but three deferrals in a row is no longer a scheduling accident, it is an unaddressed structural hole. The slug currently reaches 10 jurisdictions, ALL Anglophone-published (UK, GB-SCT, US, CA, AU, plus EN-language studies from FI, NO, CZ, FR, HK). Rest-point and public-seating provision is a domain where non-Anglophone practice is likely to differ substantively - the Nordic, German and Japanese public-realm traditions in particular - so this is a probable content gap, not merely a coverage metric.',
  'Falsified when term_aliases carries authoritative-source-verified vocabulary for at least one non-EN required language and a search on it is logged, whatever the yield.',
  '2026-07-26','session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b3','2026-07-26','session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b3','ADDRESSABLE');

